#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a0aba38-1167-5365-bbd2-cd2ba7e57b15" :question/math-academy-id "e-612" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7a39ddf2-3ba2-534f-8dca-93497cae823f" :question/math-academy-id "e-613" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6da4ce70-1718-53bb-8831-a93fdc3e4677" :question/math-academy-id "e-614" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/id #uuid "76a0fefe-71fd-5500-a4d8-7d5f8a09613e" :question/math-academy-id "e-615" :question/problem "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975930d5-fd18-51c1-8f45-7c2aa09aa645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{5t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385492} {:answer/id #uuid "7544c2eb-b2e2-54fb-aa8a-753c35a20a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385493} {:answer/id #uuid "3a82c268-1c6a-5d2e-9816-33664201353a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385494} {:answer/id #uuid "8abe4085-4103-5fb4-b936-92da9a38bf1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{2}+5,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385495} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2abbd6-0067-5ac9-8fb9-0f4954aaef26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2abbd6-0067-5ac9-8fb9-0f4954aaef26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385496} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c4e7a6-d9ee-51ba-90db-917bd21236a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "811bbc59-9fc3-5b4b-bd9e-2e09752150a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123292" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩$, then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{2t}+5,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int ({e}^{2t}+5)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{2}+5t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c9e59c-e5b1-5b66-8dff-8168e82f57e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{2}-4t,\\,\\frac{t}{8}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385499} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf1f19e-c81a-5fbe-a98b-1aac77e7abce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨t+4,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385500} {:answer/id #uuid "da6eab72-cc08-5c30-8d47-56e79e134a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}+2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385501} {:answer/id #uuid "07760852-7e75-5d60-b33c-97f4b182b3b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2{t}^{4}+2,\\,\\frac{t}{8}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385502} {:answer/id #uuid "7d279be7-88e7-5105-b1c9-f2cc00d0a788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}+2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da6eab72-cc08-5c30-8d47-56e79e134a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}+2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385501} :answer-field/id #uuid "e341e2a8-13ea-5904-bea2-edfe43b7c86c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385498}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbfe4f27-7d39-5346-b6c3-d28ca1cafdae" :question/math-academy-id "q-123294" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}+2,\\,\\frac{t}{4}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨4{t}^{3}+2,\\,\\frac{t}{4}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨4{t}^{3}+2,\\,\\frac{t}{4}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (4{t}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{t}{4}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}+2t+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}+2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}+2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{8}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101cbc3d-8ada-5787-9d21-feee751379e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332923} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce5478b-9a72-55ff-b65d-51d747a90918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332924} {:answer/id #uuid "eb066872-e293-5a52-8a19-b26ef182a5a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332925} {:answer/id #uuid "c3220efa-582f-58e2-a10e-77732718dde1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t-1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332926} {:answer/id #uuid "97612383-f607-5ead-84a2-f7aff88224f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{5t},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "101cbc3d-8ada-5787-9d21-feee751379e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332923} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a90f7e6-ebbb-53f5-b993-94997e7d0347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f7f0bed-7a5e-5c15-8327-bc7f4c63ab8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-123437" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t=⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)={e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\text{d}t={e}^{t}+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217f889b-40e9-5117-9c1a-7962c88ff7bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-64,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385506} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc0bb24-336d-54e1-af65-536fe405ef60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385507} {:answer/id #uuid "3432b9b6-ffa1-5971-810d-53c050a0c758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-45,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385508} {:answer/id #uuid "b83685af-f58f-56af-b69e-0e538eb7513b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-25,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385509} {:answer/id #uuid "b0af7050-c225-5710-92a0-deb4a76a81f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-81,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3432b9b6-ffa1-5971-810d-53c050a0c758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-45,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385508} :answer-field/id #uuid "45273d96-17c2-59e1-b8d5-9997c722bcb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a75a9ac2-e5a8-56b8-90de-02ef8cc74ba8" :question/math-academy-id "q-123456" :question/problem "${\\int }_{4}^{9}⟨4-2t,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{9}⟨4-2t,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{4}^{9}4-2t\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{4}^{9}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(4t-{t}^{2})\\,\\,{|}_{4}^{9},\\,2\\sqrt{t}\\,\\,{|}_{4}^{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-45-0,\\,6-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-45,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4445b6b7-0280-50d9-ab9d-cc1c2e794140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,5{e}^{5t}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332965} {:answer/id #uuid "7b77aede-9c55-5ec3-9e49-8d826f858596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}-2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332966} {:answer/id #uuid "cac5345a-435b-5d99-86cd-ad99e17a19b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332967} {:answer/id #uuid "34364ab1-eb6b-513e-b87a-98bf44363d25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{1/3}+1,\\,{e}^{t}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332968} {:answer/id #uuid "f05d4e77-3f85-5d2a-b440-3d79f4567766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{2t}-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cac5345a-435b-5d99-86cd-ad99e17a19b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332967} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1f277b-a634-584c-8716-a16b3efc218b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01a82786-6006-50b3-9639-081950d67e5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123474" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩$ and $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3},\\,5{e}^{5t}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{16\\sqrt[3]{t}}{3}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 5{e}^{5t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(0)=⟨2,\\,-1⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨4\\cdot {0}^{4/3}+{c}_{1},\\,{e}^{5\\cdot 0}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=2$ and ${c}_{2}=-2.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨4{t}^{4/3}+2,\\,{e}^{5t}-2⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31917785-faea-5f09-a0f2-559220ec0866" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{6}},\\,128⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385513} {:answer/id #uuid "7e921d7c-99fd-515d-b253-81d5e45ec58b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6+\\frac{1}{e},\\,228⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385514} {:answer/id #uuid "80fa8995-66fd-545f-b623-af02809e03c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-{e}^{3},\\,108⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385515} {:answer/id #uuid "04fdb09a-c318-5f03-bdc4-a424d6f68663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{6}},\\,288⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385516} {:answer/id #uuid "5249047e-e285-57a0-989e-60641a1995e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{3}},\\,280⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fdb09a-c318-5f03-bdc4-a424d6f68663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{6}},\\,288⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385516} :answer-field/id #uuid "adc140a0-5f75-55cd-a5d9-e64fb4731044" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8f25bbf-4e2b-5901-9f0f-91861655df78" :question/math-academy-id "q-123517" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{6}⟨{e}^{-t},\\,4{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}⟨{e}^{-t},\\,4{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{0}^{6}4{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(-{e}^{-t}){|}_{0}^{6},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{6}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-0},\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {6}^{3}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{6}},\\,288⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306b7cd2-f1e7-5242-ae31-dc2c614c5e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(3)-\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "306b7cd2-f1e7-5242-ae31-dc2c614c5e14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(3)-\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385520} :answer-field/id #uuid "b319d812-12ae-58e4-bcfd-41e0361de7f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385519} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "faa90b47-4de6-5f6e-8248-a02d7ab51a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faa90b47-4de6-5f6e-8248-a02d7ab51a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385522} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf928a0c-de75-55af-a690-4a47cade017b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "784dba63-554b-55cc-8825-7f46d8c83131" :question/math-academy-id "q-349112" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}⟨\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}⟨\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component, let $u=3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t$, so $\\text{d}u={csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second component, we integrate directly:\n\n$$\n\\int -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}⟨\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡t}{3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t},\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t){|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2},\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2),\\,2\\,(0-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{3}{2}),\\,-\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ln\\,(\\frac{3}{2}),\\,-\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ea0ccf0-0354-5ca9-b0ac-314907fd05fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "708" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ea0ccf0-0354-5ca9-b0ac-314907fd05fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "708" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385525} :answer-field/id #uuid "8645c0f0-97a6-5263-91ce-74241ccd029e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385524} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4724bbc-8258-5235-bb67-e3cb4e763e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4724bbc-8258-5235-bb67-e3cb4e763e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385527} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b21e01e-75d3-510d-a271-dfe9d302f54c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11c7606c-3688-541f-b65a-5626fa61655b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349116" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4}^{16}⟨6t-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{16}⟨6t-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{4}^{16}(6t-1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{4}^{16}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int (6t-1)\\,\\text{d}t=3{t}^{2}-t.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t=\\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{16}⟨6t-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(3{t}^{2}-t){|}_{4}^{16},\\,(\\sqrt{t}){|}_{4}^{16}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(3\\cdot {16}^{2}-16)-(3\\cdot {4}^{2}-4),\\,4-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(768-16)-(48-4),\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨752-44,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨708,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨708,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3081ffe7-c448-5e0d-8dd1-808d23199a7f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Definite Integral of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d1aab51-65cb-5fcc-b95b-6ee586256733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d1aab51-65cb-5fcc-b95b-6ee586256733" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385530} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ad3696c-ddc0-535e-9e05-7cf9407c510b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2da444f-5894-574e-a687-136da4e5ad37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2da444f-5894-574e-a687-136da4e5ad37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385532} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a4bf87-ed49-5dcf-98ac-d829a358ca67" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "baea03dd-15c5-569c-9f74-7ecdd75c4adb" :question/math-academy-id "q-349147" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral of a vector-valued function. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $⟩$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{4}({t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{4}(3{t}^{3}+t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first component,\n\n$$\n\\int ({t}^{2}-2t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFor the second component,\n\n$$\n\\int (3{t}^{3}+t)\\,\\text{d}t=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}⟨{t}^{2}-2t,\\,3{t}^{3}+t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4},\\,(\\frac{3}{4}{t}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{1}{3}(64)-16)-0,\\,(\\frac{3}{4}(256)+\\frac{1}{2}(16))-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨(\\frac{64}{3}-16),\\,(192+8)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{16}{3},\\,200⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{16}{3},\\,200⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97567933-d63f-59fe-ad8e-dcd05483abb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385535} {:answer/id #uuid "083d2621-f147-5cf1-b25f-dc2aa90934fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{t}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "083d2621-f147-5cf1-b25f-dc2aa90934fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{t}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385536} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dafb2dd-b14b-58c8-a1f6-e72b1e4d55e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f61c2eed-5fb3-5eb4-a54a-ef6f17075b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-2t}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f61c2eed-5fb3-5eb4-a54a-ef6f17075b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{-2t}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385538} :answer-field/id #uuid "7031045f-74ad-56d7-96cb-961ea22211a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3d00973-ef37-5914-9b0b-74027ff07272" :question/math-academy-id "q-349183" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=⟨11,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 4{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\sqrt{t}+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨11,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨6\\sqrt{1}+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨11,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3⟩ \\\\ ⟨6+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨11,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=5$ and ${c}_{2}=3.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨6\\sqrt{t}+5,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}+3⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8500ecfa-7f69-5692-8378-8a2da6c8d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8500ecfa-7f69-5692-8378-8a2da6c8d14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297320} :answer-field/id #uuid "d017f787-38e7-5ada-9e05-3e69d1b615f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4279aaa-49fe-5b0c-891a-825cbf2ec989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4279aaa-49fe-5b0c-891a-825cbf2ec989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\ln(t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297322} :answer-field/id #uuid "492cfa94-52ea-559a-bd8d-87c09d8c7730" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b119c5-e8c6-574b-9b80-220999d2b97b" :question/math-academy-id "q-349193" :question/problem "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩ \\\\ ⟨8+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-6$ and ${c}_{2}=0.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6ee661-ba22-542d-a9fb-b76d8076a27a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{1}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095702} {:answer/id #uuid "bb21cdf1-22bd-524b-852c-992658713584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095703} {:answer/id #uuid "c82b3f55-eede-588c-8f00-ece0e818fa7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- ⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095704} {:answer/id #uuid "499e839a-bf75-5fd9-bdc6-858357101649" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095705} {:answer/id #uuid "57636129-14de-554a-a121-0e8f70645831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid, \\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb21cdf1-22bd-524b-852c-992658713584" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3\\ln \\mid t \\mid,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095703} :answer-field/id #uuid "47c6edcd-4580-541c-8ae3-e21d3e20ddad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4a69144-d189-5ac0-bdfe-ac5dd5bddd37" :question/math-academy-id "q-50201" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{t},\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{3}{t},\\,\\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{3}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\frac{5}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{5}{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|,\\,-\\frac{5}{t}⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82a2d67e-13a8-5a84-ab13-c3c5e843e9db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2e^{2t},-\\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095714} {:answer/id #uuid "0399a4e6-9b75-529f-9e5b-e28dea127114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095715} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb63997-87d9-51b3-9ec9-9aac82e68587" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{2}e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095716} {:answer/id #uuid "63002e0e-db0b-5ef3-88a3-0a9902f7bfe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\cos t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095717} {:answer/id #uuid "63c5bef5-1cd5-593e-adbd-cd507df93001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2e^{t},-\\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0399a4e6-9b75-529f-9e5b-e28dea127114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨e^{t}, \\sin t⟩ + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095715} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a1bf073-4db0-5a09-aecc-ff3e23e8c2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095713}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1bad6949-79b1-5ca9-94b6-1b4bffc3a4cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-50204" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186332989 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b8e8a96-9973-5ffb-a692-45bf60b973a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332991} {:answer/id #uuid "14dd103f-69e8-5966-9e39-41a6ca90cf76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332992} {:answer/id #uuid "0edd8566-357e-5796-83ba-1da8b62e7650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332993} {:answer/id #uuid "267423a9-af09-5ebb-a456-596352097c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332994} {:answer/id #uuid "dca9ce97-ee20-5cbe-9fe4-8f2c57858563" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14dd103f-69e8-5966-9e39-41a6ca90cf76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332992} :answer-field/id #uuid "de5a67a5-0e3d-5adc-88fa-817279c40f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed9275a1-ce69-572b-90c1-a522c36d6a6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80463" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6ac72b4-fc55-5c24-91a0-7e9995c206ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}-1,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385541} {:answer/id #uuid "263a796b-776f-5aa0-8101-96956a88b3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}-t,{e}^{2t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385542} {:answer/id #uuid "cae03307-c9b3-580b-8c85-34381a8232b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3{t}^{4}-2t,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385543} {:answer/id #uuid "da83afee-1780-5d2e-95fa-1ae9f5c5bf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}-t,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385544} {:answer/id #uuid "c929992e-bce0-5bfa-9b7e-4792fae8273f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{t}^{2}-t,2{e}^{2t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da83afee-1780-5d2e-95fa-1ae9f5c5bf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{4}-t,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385544} :answer-field/id #uuid "d43fa657-4567-5305-a1a7-79ff5d4c7dc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b610ae44-a882-5221-be1d-5cbe96ffd50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-99253" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}-1,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨4{t}^{3}-1,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨4{t}^{3}-1,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (4{t}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}t,2\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}-t+{c}_{1},\\,2{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}-t,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4}-t,\\,2{e}^{t}⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9688df89-056e-59d7-869e-9841715b2aea" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca3a1815-9872-5c8c-9bf9-9f225cb9ebd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385548} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea480f9-b662-5eff-aa51-3ddec1c6a3e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385549} {:answer/id #uuid "f79a52c7-b167-58da-aaae-7e78520762cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385550} {:answer/id #uuid "b67e59fc-0131-5620-894d-4bc65cac4fac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385551} {:answer/id #uuid "4896a19a-21d3-546c-b7d3-1bbd3c443028" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f79a52c7-b167-58da-aaae-7e78520762cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385550} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded138c3-b870-5ffd-8289-991877b48eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3bcb2d31-941b-5940-a9b3-d7493de59538" :question/math-academy-id "q-99260" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{sec}^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{sec}^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{sec}^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1931dd8-7454-5ae4-9941-da525a073842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385555} {:answer/id #uuid "a8202694-f1ec-5e9d-9738-e970c6ae9033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385556} {:answer/id #uuid "1141079a-19aa-5fdd-9c7c-f2d6ad101b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385557} {:answer/id #uuid "88948b16-ddb8-5649-8a96-794616ece5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,-2{t}^{3}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385558} {:answer/id #uuid "e457e4a2-9f23-5f2c-94f5-ea4af362203d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8202694-f1ec-5e9d-9738-e970c6ae9033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a86665ce-7f9a-5213-890c-a18c738dc168" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d413689c-9799-50bd-948a-f60e39c1c13a" :question/math-academy-id "q-99352" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}⟩\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int -\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186333017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c45f96d-03b1-5bd6-bb3a-31d5d9f60d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{({e}^{2t}+e)}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333019} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b1a71d-f4b0-5165-94b6-4b0e922559d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333020} {:answer/id #uuid "166a60e6-716c-551b-a7dd-3beb0c13fae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333021} {:answer/id #uuid "bcefa098-1f2f-539a-970b-dabe8993220c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} {:answer/id #uuid "728197e8-77cf-5e4a-a9a8-bb0d0d95bf18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{2t}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcefa098-1f2f-539a-970b-dabe8993220c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333022} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b09ba27-ddf7-5f44-89a9-f9023f3c7f27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb6f108b-b2c6-57c1-9132-69c2656eace2" :question/math-academy-id "q-99378" :question/problem "Find $\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=2{e}^{(2t+1)},$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{u}+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3a99672-6130-5757-97a9-b83c8b12152d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297366} {:answer/id #uuid "c1352cdf-a45a-5473-8cb5-e42a88c50278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297367} {:answer/id #uuid "754a9675-1fba-57e7-b5df-c41e907a83ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{4}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297368} {:answer/id #uuid "647b7987-adbd-5e6d-92f8-a6c276eebf61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297369} {:answer/id #uuid "c94e23ed-1753-5650-a1c1-b6caad8e1766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{t}^{3}+2,\\,{t}^{4}{-}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1352cdf-a45a-5473-8cb5-e42a88c50278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c88d0d3d-3348-569a-ae2e-19e781544506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ac793faa-32dd-5854-af7f-a8fbffd850cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-99517" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3(t-1)^{2},4\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3(t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (4{t}^{3}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{4}-t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨{((1)-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{4}-(1)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dd18a5b-d7a1-5590-ae70-f47ff5b464b1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Vector-Valued Function That Satisfies a Given Initial Condition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df8955f2-9a32-5b17-8bff-248f3d27d7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-1,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385562} {:answer/id #uuid "97b4223c-7d99-53b6-b68c-8d022f820fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+1,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385563} {:answer/id #uuid "9c490178-18aa-5391-ad88-0680d15ee0d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1-t|,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385564} {:answer/id #uuid "76c102f6-6195-5616-9b74-041dff9d66d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385565} {:answer/id #uuid "59963ef5-5a1f-5633-ac55-771559b01186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+1,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df8955f2-9a32-5b17-8bff-248f3d27d7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-1,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385562} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fab8a1c-c3a8-5595-ba42-a9a4539ebbe1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e321419c-a366-5737-8cc6-0eb09e45ddb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-99546" :question/problem "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨-1,\\,2⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\frac{1}{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi t)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨-1,\\,2⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|+{c}_{1},\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,1+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨-1,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡|t|-1,\\,1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)⟩.\n$$"}]}
